                          "index":  0,
                          "text":  "My friends call me Oppy. I landed on January 25, 2004, three weeks after my twin, Spirit. My airbags bounced me across a flat plain and dropped me into a small crater. A hole in one. And right there in the crater wall was the layered rock my team had dreamed of.\n\nIn those rocks I found little round pebbles, like blueberries in a muffin. They are made of a mineral that forms in water. Within two months I had my answer: this dry plain was once soaked.",
